{
 "area": "corebridge/js/host-prolog-engine.js — core's PrologEngine seam over libinsimul",
 "description": "PL.native-consult-floor-leak. Each step runs on the shipped engine and on the rebuild-only oracle (the pre-change code, in driver.js); their answers, and every probe's answers, must be identical JSON (order counts) unless a step says oracleDiffers. expect is the stated answer for any runner; cost bounds the step's native work: creates = KBs created, maxConsultBytes = the largest single consult in bytes. kbSlots bounds the bridge's KB table. The fuzz block is a seeded LCG op sequence over its pools (driver.js runFuzz), compared after every op. A consult step's cost counts KBs created by the step itself: a new engine's first consult reuses the KB createPrologEngine made (creates 0). destroy releases the engine's KB and its program, rules and facts (it reports what it still holds) and ends the case.",
 "cases": [
  {
   "name": "a skill take in a held village-sized KB: each fact write creates no KB and consults only its own text",
   "probes": [
    "skill_points(A, T, P)",
    "skill_unlocked(A, N)",
